.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-TRUST-CERT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-trust-cert
.Nd make Chrome and Firefox trust the machine's certificate authority
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl -system
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Browsers on Linux do not read the system trust store; each user's browser
reads its own NSS database,
.Pa ~/.pki/nssdb .
.Nm
adds the machine's root certificate,
.Pa /etc/kldload/ca/root/ca.crt
from
.Xr kldload-ca 8 ,
to that database, trusted to issue server certificates, so the web
console and everything else the authority signs open without a warning.
.Pp
It adds the root, not the console's own certificate: that one is replaced
whenever the machine's addresses change, and a trusted copy of it would
stop matching.
.Pp
It does nothing to a database that already trusts the current root.
A database that holds an older root, or the right one with the wrong trust
flags, has the entry replaced.
An entry named
.Ql kldload-webui ,
left by installs that trusted the console's certificate directly, is
removed.
.Pp
Without arguments it updates the invoking user's database, creating it if
there is none; the desktop runs it this way at every login.
With
.Fl -system ,
run as root, it updates
.Pa /etc/skel ,
so users created later start with the root trusted,
.Pa /root ,
and every directory under
.Pa /home ,
as the user who owns it.
.Pa kldload-tls-cert.service
runs it so each time it runs.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -system
Every user's database, as described above.
Needs root.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kldload/ca/root/ca.crt
The root it trusts; if that is missing,
.Pa /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/kldload-ca.crt .
.It Pa ~/.pki/nssdb/
A user's browser trust database.
.It Pa /etc/xdg/autostart/kldload-trust-cert.desktop
Runs it at each desktop login.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Every database trusts the root, or there is no root or no
.Xr certutil 1
to do it with, which it says.
.It 1
A database could not be updated;
.Fl -system
goes on to the others first and then says how many failed.
.Fl -system
run as a user.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on 2026-09-30 in a Fedora 44 container with a throwaway authority
and one user,
.Ql alice .
.Ss Before there is an authority
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-trust-cert --system
kldload-trust-cert: no kldload CA root at /etc/kldload/ca/root/ca.crt; nothing to trust
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Ss Every user, then again
After
.Ql kldload-ca init :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-trust-cert --system
kldload-trust-cert: imported kldload-ca (5E4495E5F8A71409...) into /etc/skel/.pki/nssdb
kldload-trust-cert: imported kldload-ca (5E4495E5F8A71409...) into /root/.pki/nssdb
kldload-trust-cert: imported kldload-ca (5E4495E5F8A71409...) into /home/alice/.pki/nssdb
# (exited 0)
# su - alice -c 'certutil -L -d sql:$HOME/.pki/nssdb'

Certificate Nickname                                         Trust Attributes
                                                             SSL,S/MIME,JAR/XPI

kldload-ca                                                   CT,C,
# (exited 0)
# kldload-trust-cert --system
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
The second run had nothing to do.
.Ss A database it cannot write
After
.Ql kldload-ca init --force
made a new root, with alice's database made read-only:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-trust-cert --system
kldload-trust-cert: imported kldload-ca (630CD6178BD9D72F...) into /etc/skel/.pki/nssdb
kldload-trust-cert: imported kldload-ca (630CD6178BD9D72F...) into /root/.pki/nssdb
certutil: function failed: SEC_ERROR_READ_ONLY: security library: read-only database.
kldload-trust-cert: FAILED to import kldload-ca into /home/alice/.pki/nssdb
kldload-trust-cert: 1 database(s) NOT updated; see above
# (exited 1)
# su - alice -c kldload-trust-cert
certutil: function failed: SEC_ERROR_READ_ONLY: security library: read-only database.
kldload-trust-cert: FAILED to import kldload-ca into /home/alice/.pki/nssdb
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr certutil 1 ,
.Xr kldload-ca 8 ,
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8
.Sh HISTORY
It first trusted the console's certificate, and the warning came back each
time that certificate was replaced (seen 2026-07-28).
On 2026-06-09 the copy run for each user was found to be given no trust
flags, so every browser window of the console opened on the warning.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: a database it could not write was
reported as
.Dq imported
and the run exited 0, because its callers ignored the failure; and it
exited 0 without a word when there was no authority.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Only
.Pa /root
and directories directly under
.Pa /home
are visited; a user whose home is elsewhere is updated at their next
desktop login.
.Pp
The system trust store, which
.Xr curl 1
and most programs use, is
.Xr kldload-ca 8 Ns 's
.Cm trust-install ,
not this.
